#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087759 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "54588722-bb80-54ca-b100-03aca39e0c17" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Argument of a Complex Number in the Fourth Quadrant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa713718-4023-5280-813d-3aa91128a3be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa713718-4023-5280-813d-3aa91128a3be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.62" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232408} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bdc18ae-186c-5350-9538-a2d1a6ea5f2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c91f4f8-2fbe-5963-a53b-2aead62a5f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275159" :question/problem "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=9-7\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$\\operatorname{arg}(z)\\approx $\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](images/b6/b6ec4332891a4c7684be8de2ca94bf24a1d9abd5170d9fe38ad3a1346afae56a.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<\\operatorname{arg}(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =\\operatorname{arctan}(\\frac{7}{9})=0.661\\,043…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}(z)=2\\pi -0.661\\,043\\approx 5.62,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."}]}
